  "generated_text": "To find the ordered pair $(s, l)$, we need to match the given parametric form of the line with the standard equation of the line.\n\nThe parametric form of the line is given by:\n\\[\\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -7 \\\\ s \\end{pmatrix} + t \\begin{pmatrix} l \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\n\nWe can rewrite this as:\n\\[x = -7 + tl\\]\n\\[y = s - 5t.\\]\n\nComparing this with the standard equation of the line $y = \\frac{1}{2} x + 4$, we can equate the coefficients of $x$ and $y$:\n\\[l = \\frac{1}{2}\\]\n\\[s = 4\\]\n\nTherefore, the ordered pair $(s, l)$ is:\n\\[(s, l) = \\boxed{(4, \\frac{1}{2})}.\\]The answer is: (4,\\frac{1}{2})",
